{"audit_id": "c332f27ec2db0603", "audited_at": "2026-11-26T15:12:48.877114+00:00", "depth": "full_manuscript", "description_sha256": "c712ec2f3eac5c8b67eb07de988769dd0c4739486d9c4094704300f286a617d5", "lecture_id": "014000", "manuscript_sha256": "7781be1283c7b503ba9bcc3c9023f284301986c4769fc064cee85fb895e5db1a", "note": "The current summary omitted substantial Hagar/Ishmael material, the binding of Isaac and the two marriages of Jacob. The lecture also examines Abraham's argument about divine judgment, the boundary pact, Esau's embrace and the violence against Shechem after Dinah's violation. Place labels refer to the received story; Moriah and Peniel are not pinned to specific modern sites. Entire spoken manuscript reviewed against title, description, topical tags, tag paths and places. Chronology and independent source verification outside scope.", "outcome": "corrected", "reviewer": {"kind": "model", "model": "GPT-6.2", "name": null}, "schema": 2, "scope": ["description", "title", "tags", "tag_paths", "geography"], "scope_outcomes": {"description": "corrected", "geography": "corrected", "tag_paths": "corrected", "tags": "corrected", "title": "clean"}, "scope_sha256": {"description": "c712ec2f3eac5c8b67eb07de988769dd0c4739486d9c4094704300f286a617d5", "geography": "c4948f410c6482dcb0e7e96de197f48610863d574a485ffadc3ee516fb30e5fe", "tag_paths": "b760513c6e37a8e25e31dc99f9d3e43f8c6117db3d13475ec2dd6834cda0f452", "tags": "8704785d78b033f60a0150c8c8ae9c4241b9a472e6dff2ecf65efa8fb48873dd", "title": "3aaa31e0c48d8256e3b5d3565775daec2e5b192e705127ada5aaac821c626f31"}, "track": "literature-survey", "verification_basis": "manuscript_alignment"}
